{
  "description": "Single-threaded vfhe measurements (Intel(R) Xeon(R) Platinum 8488C, engine _vfhe_native_avx512ifma.lib, vfhe 83a59f7), over R_q with N = 2^13, three 45-bit primes and splitting degree 4. Times in milliseconds by log2 of the input size in R_q elements, each the minimum over its runs. Basefold uses the general foldable code with twists in F_(p^4), and the estimator's k0, n0 and query repetitions; commit and every proof include the Merkle hashing, which merkle times alone for the commitment. basefold_eval is one claim at a point of random R_q coordinates. batchfold_batching is BatchFold's evaluation of one claim at a point of exceptional coordinates, where vfhe skips the common-point sumcheck; sumcheck is a degree-2 sumcheck over R_q (SumcheckProd, two tables).",
